From 1d45dfc41e161ec23d40ed569c201b19d6f3ab36 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:58:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(motion): the lifted-return law reads the stock
 through Stock, not Dexel

The trochoid's lifted_cut still took a raw Dexel, but since #783 its stock
comes from quality::stock_for as a Stock. It now walks the stock with
Stock::subtract_flat and reads it through Columns. A stock the reading
cannot serve is a named refusal, never a pass.

Refs #844

